  headers). Text: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.txt

tools/ttimage/md5.c, tools/ttimage/md5.h
  MD5 by Colin Plumb, 1993. The header says no copyright is claimed and the
  code is in the public domain.

tools/ttimage/mkttimage.c
  "TomTom Go Firmware generator", (C) 2004 Thomas Kleffel.
  GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later
  version (stated in the file header). Built together with the Blowfish code
  above.

workspace/gui/font_data.h, workspace/gui/OFL.txt
  Glyph tables generated from Roboto, Copyright 2011 The Roboto Project
  Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/roboto-classic).
  SIL Open Font License 1.1 (workspace/gui/OFL.txt).
  tools/gui-assets/fetch.sh downloads the pinned font and its OFL.txt into
  build/gui-assets/ (not committed).

workspace/gui/icon_data.h, tools/gui-assets/gen_icons.py
  Icon bitmaps generated from Material Design Icons (@mdi/svg 7.4.47,
  https://pictogrammers.com/library/mdi/). The header states the icons are
  licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
  Text: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

brand/fonts/*.ttf, brand/fonts/OFL.txt, workspace/gui/wordmark_data.h
  Poppins, Copyright 2020 The Poppins Project Authors
  (https://github.com/itfoundry/Poppins).
  SIL Open Font License 1.1 (brand/fonts/OFL.txt). The fonts are unchanged.
  The wordmark bitmap table in wordmark_data.h is derived from Poppins
  SemiBold.

kernel/patches/, kernel/homtom/, kernel/modules/
  Patches and new files for the Linux kernel, version 6.1. They are derived
  from or built into the kernel and are GPL-2.0-only. The kernel itself is not
  included; it is fetched from kernel.org at build time.

Open points
===========

- icon_data.h is derived from Apache-2.0 icons (Material Design Icons); the
  Apache-2.0 text is in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.
- The 2004 TomTom image extractor (ttimgextract) is not included because its
  source states no licence.
- Files without an SPDX-License-Identifier line fall under the split in
  LICENSE by directory. Third-party headers above take precedence.
